{"author":"schacon+claude-opus@gmail.com","body":"de14075ad; 16/16 passing. Root causes (grit/src/commands/): (1) tests 6/7 — CLI glob fetch skipped FETCH_HEAD push on up-to-date refs, so an all-unchanged fetch fell back to listing all heads, ignoring the negative refspec; now emit FETCH_HEAD before the up-to-date continue. (2) test 11 — prune ignored negatives; added local_ref_protected_by_negative (mirrors git refspec_find_negative_match) threaded into prune_stale_refs. (3) tests 12/13 — matching push counted matched refs after negative exclusion, wrongly erroring 'No refs in common'; count both-sides refs before excluding so all-excluded push is a no-op success. (4) test 14 — prefetch ran on normalized dst (bogus/* -> refs/heads/bogus/*) yielding refs/prefetch/heads/...; added collect_refspecs_for_prefetch operating on raw config dst. No regressions: t5510 11->11, t5505 62->61, t5516 118->118."}